  "result": "Perfect! All 46 tests pass. Here's what I added:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Added two functions to `src/invoices.js`:**\n\n1. **`lineTotal(line)`** \u2014 calculates `qty \u00d7 unitPrice`\n   - Returns `ok(roundCents(result))`\n   - Validates line has both `qty` and `unitPrice` as numbers\n   - Returns `fail('LINE_INVALID')` for bad input\n\n2. **`invoiceTotals(invoice)`** \u2014 calculates subtotal and total\n   - Returns `ok({ subtotal, total })` where `subtotal` is the sum of all line totals\n   - `total` equals `subtotal` for now (discounts and VAT coming later)\n   - Validates invoice has a non-empty `lines` array\n   - Returns `fail('INVOICE_INVALID')` for bad input\n   - Propagates errors from `lineTotal()` if any line is invalid\n\n**Updated `src/errors.js`** with two new codes:\n- `LINE_INVALID` \u2014 for lines missing qty or unitPrice\n- `INVOICE_INVALID` \u2014 for invoices with missing or empty lines\n\n**Added 20 comprehensive tests** covering:\n- Line total calculations with various quantities (including zero and large numbers)\n- Invoice totals with single and multiple lines\n- Input validation for both functions\n- Error propagation\n- Integration with real invoices from `createInvoice()`\n\nAll 46 tests pass \u2705",
